description:
Design a read-only memory (ROM) module that outputs a 4-bit value based on a 4-bit input address. The module maps specific addresses to predefined data values: when the address is 0, it outputs 3; for address 1, it outputs 2; for address 2, it outputs 1; and for any other address, it outputs 0. This functionality is beneficial for applications needing fixed data retrieval based on input addresses.
module top_module(
    addr,
    dout
);

code:
module top_module(
    addr,
    dout
);input [3:0] addr;
output [3:0] dout;
reg [3:0] dout;




always @(addr) begin: ROMPARMLOAD_READACTION
    case (addr)
        0: dout = 3;
        1: dout = 2;
        2: dout = 1;
        default: dout = 0;
    endcase
end

endmodule

