description:
Develop a circuit that functions as a 4-to-1 multiplexer with 12 one-bit inputs, where the selection is controlled by a single bit (S). The module takes a 12-bit input (I) and routes one of the four possible 3-bit segments of the input to the output (O), specifically the most significant bit (MSB) of the selected segment. The selection logic is based on the value of S, effectively determining which segment is passed to the output.
module top_module(
  input [11:0] I,
  input S,
  output O
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [11:0] I,
  input S,
  output O
);wire [3:0] select = {S, S, S, S};
  wire [3:0] not_select = ~select;
  wire [11:0] selected_inputs = (select & I) | (not_select & I[11:0]);

  assign O = selected_inputs[11];

endmodule

