Design a circuit that functions as an LED driver, controlling multiple outputs based on a set of input signals and an enable signal. The module receives four input signals and produces eight output signals connected to LEDs. When the enable signal is active, specific outputs mirror the corresponding input signals or generate combinations of them using Boolean operations. If the enable signal is low, all outputs are turned off, ensuring that the LEDs remain inactive.
