description:
Design a delay circuit that introduces a delay of a specified number of clock cycles to a single-bit input signal A. This module utilizes a shift register (buffer) to hold the input value, and the output X reflects the input signal A delayed by DELAY_CYCLES clock cycles. When the clock transitions, the latest input A is shifted into the buffer, while the output takes the value of the last element in the buffer, effectively creating a delay effect.
module top_module(
    input  A,
    input  clk,         // Added clk as an input
    output X
);

code:
module top_module(
    input  A,
    input  clk,         // Added clk as an input
    output X
);parameter DELAY_CYCLES = 10;

    reg [DELAY_CYCLES-1:0] buffer;
    wire delayed_A;

    assign delayed_A = buffer[DELAY_CYCLES-1];

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        buffer <= {buffer[DELAY_CYCLES-2:0], A};
    end

    assign X = delayed_A;

endmodule

