description:
Create a 4-to-2 priority encoder that outputs the position of the highest-order active input bit. The module takes a 4-bit input and, based on which single input bit is high, assigns its corresponding position (0 to 3) to a 2-bit wide output. If no input bits are active, the output defaults to position 0.
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] pos
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [3:0] in,
  output reg [1:0] pos
);always @*
  begin
    case(in)
      4'b0001: pos = 0;
      4'b0010: pos = 1;
      4'b0100: pos = 2;
      4'b1000: pos = 3;
      default: pos = 0;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

