description:
Design a circuit that calculates the integer square root of an 8-bit input value using the Newton-Raphson iterative method. The module takes an 8-bit binary input and estimates the square root, updating the estimate until the difference between successive estimates is minimal. The final result is output as an 8-bit binary value, indicating the integer part of the square root of the input. A done flag is included to indicate when the calculation has completed.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] x,
  output [7:0] y
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] x,
  output [7:0] y
);reg [7:0] y_n; // current estimate of square root
  reg [7:0] y_n1; // next estimate of square root
  reg [7:0] x_int; // integer representation of input
  reg done; // flag to indicate when calculation is complete

  // convert binary input to integer
  assign x_int = $unsigned(x);

  // initialize y(0) to 128
  initial y_n = 128;

  always @(*) begin
    // calculate y(n+1) using Newton-Raphson method
    y_n1 = (y_n + x_int/y_n)/2;

    // check if y(n+1) and y(n) are within 1 of each other
    if (y_n1 >= y_n-1 && y_n1 <= y_n+1) begin
      done = 1; // calculation is complete
    end else begin
      y_n = y_n1; // update current estimate
      done = 0; // calculation is not yet complete
    end
  end

  // convert final estimate of square root back to binary and output it
  assign y = $unsigned(y_n1);

endmodule

